        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Calculate  <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Calculate [MATH: \\displaystyle{\\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we let <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u=1-3x,]</span> then</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.]</span></p><p>Then, we can write the integral in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u]</span> and evaluate:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222be^{1 \u2212 3x}dx|= \u222be^{u} \u22c5 (\u2212 (1)/(3))du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)\u222be^{u}du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{u} + C; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{1 \u2212 3x} + C]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "If we let [MATH: u=1-3x,] then\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.]\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of [MATH: u] and evaluate:\n\n[MATH: \u222be^{1 \u2212 3x}dx|= \u222be^{u} \u22c5 (\u2212 (1)/(3))du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)\u222be^{u}du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{u} + C; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{1 \u2212 3x} + C]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle{\\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nIf we let [MATH: u=1-3x,] then\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.]\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of [MATH: u] and evaluate:\n\n[MATH: \u222be^{1 \u2212 3x}dx|= \u222be^{u} \u22c5 (\u2212 (1)/(3))du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)\u222be^{u}du; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{u} + C; = \u2212 (1)/(3)e^{1 \u2212 3x} + C]"
      },
